  "description": "A genocide whose footage doesn't exist is rebuilt in clay. Panh's family died under the Khmer Rouge; the propaganda reels show smiling peasants, so he carves little clay figures and dioramas to stand where the record is missing. The archive that exists, set against the reality that went unrecorded — and it is a documentary.\n\nRithy Panh uses clay figures, archival footage, and his narration to recreate the atrocities Cambodia's Khmer Rouge committed between 1975 and 1979.",
